Native mapping (as in option 1), plus:

  GuardrailTriggered  -> RAW { event: <AgentEvent JSON verbatim> }
  ApprovalRequested   -> RAW { event: ... }
  PermissionDenied    -> RAW { event: ... }
  HandoffItem         -> RAW { event: ... }
  RepairStarted       -> RAW { event: ... }
  StructuredOutputFailed -> RAW { event: ... }

Lossless, no invented names.
But RAW is spec'd for upstream-provider passthrough:
frameworks surface it as opaque debug data, so a UI
is unlikely to render an approval prompt from it.

